---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../styles/routes.css';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Kavish Singh and his one-person design and software studio in Sacramento, California."
>
  <article class="route-page page-container route-page--about">
    <header class="route-intro">
      <p class="route-kicker">About</p>
      <h1>One person, from first mark to working tool.</h1>
      <p>I run Nexus Vantage Group from Sacramento, California. I design, build and look after work that crosses print, websites and software.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="route-prose">
      <section aria-labelledby="about-client-work">
        <h2 id="about-client-work">Client work</h2>
        <p>I work with businesses on the things their customers see and use. I built a local retail store's website from the ground up, including its customer file-upload portal for print orders. The store's customer PC with timed, card-paid plans is still in progress.</p>
        <p>I have also built the live Bandola Brews website. My work for Compassion Care &amp; Transport Services is in progress. I describe private staff tools without showing their screens.</p>
        <a href="/projects/web-design">See client work</a>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="about-own-tools">
        <h2 id="about-own-tools">Tools I make</h2>
        <p>I build software for my own work too. Cokpit is an in-progress desktop app for supervising AI coding agent sessions side by side. NVG Voice is a Windows dictation tool I built and use daily.</p>
        <a href="/projects/prospect">See products</a>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="about-print-work">
        <h2 id="about-print-work">Print and care</h2>
        <p>I began with print design and still make room for it in this practice. The pieces in my print portfolio are designs I made while employed at a retail store; they are not Nexus Vantage Group client projects.</p>
        <p>I can carry a job from identity and printed material into a website or app, then handle the updates, fixes and infrastructure I run. Each inquiry can cover one part or several.</p>
        <a href="/projects/graphic-design">See print work</a>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="route-action" aria-label="Start an inquiry">
      <p>Have a job in mind?</p>
      <a href="/contact">Start a ticket <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </aside>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
